From fcdb87dc6f05ec64cdc96ffb7e697d95a486ffab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nipuna H Herath <nipunaherath@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:57:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] CUDA/HIP: Inkling 2's attention output projection and
 its conv step as one kernel

The attention output projection (a BF16 product on one F32 vector) was
followed by the one-token conv step on its result (the step's new column and
its residual) and, now inside that step, the layer residual. A block per
output row now computes the row with mul_mat_vec_f's arithmetic (its block
size, reduction order and the two idle RDNA4 blocks for a multiple of 256
rows), then that channel's conv step, state store and residual, so the
output is bit-identical.

R9700 Inkling-2-Mini UD-Q8_K_XL: 1,281 -> 1,233 kernels per generated token;
tg128 61.0 -> 62.1 tok/s. KLD against the previous commit, wiki.test.raw
-c 512, -ub 512 and -ub 1: 0. test-backend-ops SSM_CONV_STEP gains cases
with a 3072 x 2304 BF16 product as the step's input.
